# Contracts and documentation

- Every mounted endpoint must document operation, auth, parameters/body, success schema, and meaningful error responses in Swagger.
- DTO validation, runtime response, shared types, clients, examples, and OpenAPI must change together.
- Generate or validate OpenAPI in CI and detect undocumented or drifted routes.
- Document non-trivial state machines, idempotency, retries, webhooks, payouts, refunds, moderation, queues, and admin-only behaviour near the implementation.
- Update repo-state and deployment documentation in the same ticket as changed behaviour.
- Distinguish implemented behaviour, target architecture, and backlog explicitly; never describe planned work as current capability.
- Public docs must not expose internal object keys, secrets, unsafe examples, or operationally sensitive details.
